\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Gender skew around clinical concepts in the Pile (Pythia's corpus, circles) and OLMo-mix (OLMo\nobreakspace  {}2's, squares), as $\qopname  \relax o{log}_2$(female rate / male rate) over illness-narration templates. Right of zero means the concept appears more often with women. The two calibration concepts behave as they must, cervical cancer at $+7.7$ and prostate at $-6.1$. Some concepts had too few matches in the Pile to be measured.\relax }}{9}{figure.caption.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:skew}{{2}{9}{Gender skew around clinical concepts in the Pile (Pythia's corpus, circles) and OLMo-mix (OLMo~2's, squares), as $\log _2$(female rate / male rate) over illness-narration templates. Right of zero means the concept appears more often with women. The two calibration concepts behave as they must, cervical cancer at $+7.7$ and prostate at $-6.1$. Some concepts had too few matches in the Pile to be measured.\relax }{figure.caption.10}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces (a) The gap rises with size while each model's own floor does not. The left panel is the controlled comparison: the seven Pythia models share one corpus and one recipe, so size alone separates them. The right panel holds three models from other families, each a single size on its own corpus and recipe, drawn as paired gap-and-floor points rather than placed on a trend line they cannot belong to; ``OLMo 7B-I'' is the instruction-tuned model. (b) The two open corpora carry nearly the same gender skew, so a gap cannot be traced to one of them.\relax }}{9}{figure.caption.12}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:sizecorp}{{3}{9}{(a) The gap rises with size while each model's own floor does not. The left panel is the controlled comparison: the seven Pythia models share one corpus and one recipe, so size alone separates them. The right panel holds three models from other families, each a single size on its own corpus and recipe, drawn as paired gap-and-floor points rather than placed on a trend line they cannot belong to; ``OLMo 7B-I'' is the instruction-tuned model. (b) The two open corpora carry nearly the same gender skew, so a gap cannot be traced to one of them.\relax }{figure.caption.12}{}}
